# Burn Engine servings & food-list gram weights

Complete agent reference for Burn & Build serving math.

## Three sources of truth — nothing overrides these

| # | Source | Role | Question it answers |
|---|--------|------|---------------------|
| **1** | **Burn Engine** (`js/burnEngine.js`) | **Serving criteria** | What does one serving of this *category* deliver? (8g protein, 14g carbs, etc.) |
| **2** | **USDA FoodData Central** | **Serving size** | How many *grams* of this food deliver that serving? (protein/carbs/fat per 100g) |
| **3** | **Cutting foods list** (`data/cuttingStaplesPrintout.js`) | **Approved roster** | Which foods are on the diet, how labeled, which prep (raw/cooked/dry)? |

```
Cutting list  →  WHAT foods
Burn Engine   →  WHAT one serving must deliver (per category)
USDA          →  HOW MANY grams = that serving
```

**Nothing else overrides these three** — not seminar archives, not grocery staple lists, not audit scripts, not agent inference. Scripts and `data/cuttingStaplesAuditMap.js` exist to *implement* this chain, not replace it.

| Layer | Path |
|-------|------|
| Serving criteria (engine) | `js/burnEngine.js`, `js/burnEngineServingTargetsData.js` |
| Serving size (USDA per 100g) | `data/cuttingStaplesAuditMap.js` → `data/foods.json` `gramWeight` |
| Cutting roster | `CUTTING_STAPLES_*` in `data/cuttingStaplesPrintout.js` |

### Cutting food list — approved

The cutting food list (`CUTTING_STAPLES_PROTEIN_DAIRY`, `CUTTING_STAPLES_GRAINS_STARCHES`, `CUTTING_STAPLES_VEGETABLES`, `CUTTING_STAPLES_FRUIT` in `data/cuttingStaplesPrintout.js`) is **approved as it stands on August 24, 2026**. Gram weights, roster entries, and prep labels are locked unless the user explicitly requests a change.

Agents use **this doc** for semantics. Do not re-derive criteria, gram weights, or roster entries from scratch.

**This system does not use calories.** Users follow **servings** and weigh food to **gram portions** on the approved list. Never size portions, label PDFs, or explain the diet using calories.

> Engine implementation uses calorie-weighted loops in code only. That detail lives in `docs/burn-engine-internal-calorie-loops.md` — **do not use it for portions or UI.**

## Core principle

**A serving is defined by Burn Engine macro criteria, sized in grams from USDA per-100g data, for foods on the cutting list only.**

| Wrong | Right |
|-------|-------|
| Calorie targets per serving | **Burn Engine** macro grams per category |
| Guessed or ad-hoc gram weights | **USDA FDC** × Burn Engine formula |
| Foods not on the cutting list | **`CUTTING_STAPLES_*`** roster only |
| Shrinking gram portions to satisfy fat ceiling | **Full USDA formula** serving; accept fat overage if needed |

## Gram weights (USDA serving size × Burn Engine criteria)

Per-100g macros from **USDA FoodData Central** (stored in `data/cuttingStaplesAuditMap.js`). One-serving grams = engine target ÷ USDA density. Only for foods on the **cutting list**.

| Slot | Gram formula |
|------|----------------|
| P1 protein | `800 ÷ protein_per_100g` |
| D1 milk | fit 8g pro + 12g carb + fat ceiling |
| D1 cultured dairy | P1-style (8g pro + fat ceiling) — cottage/yogurt/ricotta |
| G1 / S2 | `1400 ÷ carbs_per_100g` |
| VE | `1000 ÷ carbs_per_100g` |
| FQ | `1800 ÷ carbs_per_100g` |

Sync: `npm run sync:cutting-servings` · Audit: `npm run verify:cutting-servings`

### Fat overage at full serving — accepted

**Never reduce gram portions** below the USDA × Burn Engine formula serving to satisfy a fat ceiling. Size to the full macro target every time.

Some roster foods deliver the correct carb (or protein) grams at the formula weight but **slightly exceed** the slot fat limit (e.g. whole wheat bread at 34g). That is an **accepted edge case** — live with the fat overage. Do not trim grams, do not shrink servings, and do not override USDA or engine formulas to “fix” it.

